		("AUDIO-018", "a positioned mono voice follows the software channel stage of QMixer.dll, which tp.exe selects for every voice (the request flag 1 is ORed in unconditionally at 0x6bc61b, so 0x6d23ab hands QSWaveMixConfigureChannel the mode 0x1000000, whose buffers have no DirectSound 3D object): the source's offset is rotated into the listener's basis (front and up from the camera matrix rows 0x7909b0 and 0x7909a0, right = up x front, 0x1800ce70, 0x1800cf10; the adapters' swap of y and z, 0x6d2640, 0x6d2a10, 0x6d2b20, and QMixer's negation of the third component, 0x18001020, make a rotation, so the camera axes need no mapping), the azimuth atan2(x, z) in degrees (0x1800cb10) becomes a DirectSound pan of 44.444 hundredths of a dB per degree mirrored behind the listener (0x18005730), the gain a volume of 2000 log10(gain) hundredths of a dB (0x1800ca40), and 0x18005830 sets the volume for every wave and the pan for a mono wave only (the format table 0x1803c6b4 test at 0x1800597c-0x1800599f gates only the SetPan); the opposite channel is 10^(-|pan|/2000) of the level; a voice with the any-distance flag (event flag 0x200, speech, music, most interface sounds) is placed flat by the library (0x6bc51d: QSWaveMixSetPosition with the integers 0, 1, 0, 0x18007abd) and is centred at the voice's own gain. Doppler is read: every voice without the loop flag (voice flag 4 makes the request flag 0x40 through 0x6bc628 -> 0x6c5110, which 0x6d22d0 turns into the channel's no-Doppler bit 0x10, tested at 0x1800a1df) takes the factor 1 / (1 + x), x = (direction . relative velocity) / 331.36 (the engine's speed-of-sound scales +0x88 and +0x90 are 1.0 from the table 0x180311f0; tp.exe imports QSWaveMixSetSpeedOfSound but its adapter 0x6d2ce0 is never called), at most 10 (0x1800a178-0x1800a2c3), which 0x18005550 multiplies into the stream frequency (an integer, 0x180055c8-0x180055dd) while the voice's first stream reader has its decoder (0x18005599-0x180055bd: +0x90 set, which the library's